e</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Three dimensional structure of human C-reactive protein</article-title><source>Nat Struct Biol</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>346</fpage><lpage>354</lpage><year>1996</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8599761</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Pepys</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The physiological structure of human C-reactive protein and its complex with phosphocholine</article-title><source>Structure</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>169</fpage><lpage>177</lpage><year>1999</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10368284</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bang</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Analysis of binding sites in human C-reactive protein for Fc{gamma}RI, Fc{gamma}RIIA, and C1q by site-directed mutagenesis</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>280</volume><fpage>25095</fpage><lpage>25102</lpage><year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15878871</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tax</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Willems</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Reekers</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Capel</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Koene</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Polymorphism in mitogenic effect of IgG1 monoclonal antibodies against T3 antigen on human T cells</art